        {
            "_id": "tdKFDOnYDakP5wSN",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Hellfire Blast",
            "sort": 500000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The thruneosaurus channels sulfurous hellfire in one of three ways. The thruneosaurus chooses the effect, but it can't make the same choice in two consecutive rounds.</p><ul><li><strong>Blistering Sun</strong> (divine, fire, unholy) The thruneosaurus ignites an orb of hellfire between its horns that radiates heat in a @Template[emanation|distance:30], dealing @Damage[2d8[persistent,fire]] damage.</li><li><strong>Choking Fumes</strong> (divine, poison, unholy) The thruneosaurus exhales a @Template[cone|distance:60] of sulfurous smoke that deals @Damage[6d8[poison]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:38|traits:divine,poison,unholy|basic|options:area-effect] save). Creatures that fail their saves are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened]{Sickened 2}.</li><li><strong>Fiery Beam</strong> (divine, fire, unholy) A @Template[line|distance:120] of hellish flame erupts from the thruneosaurus's eyes, dealing @Damage[6d10[fire]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:38|traits:divine,fire,unholy|basic|options:area-effect] save).</li></ul>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
